<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Open Notes – Message-Queue</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/message-queue/</link><description>Recent content in Message-Queue on Open Notes</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 01 May 2025 00:00:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/message-queue/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Ripple MQ: High-Performance Distributed Event Streaming</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/ripple/</link><pubDate>Thu, 01 May 2025 00:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/ripple/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/ripple-mq/ripple-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub (Server)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/ripple-mq/go-client" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub (Go Client)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/ripple-mq/benchmark" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub (Benchmark)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ripple MQ&lt;/strong&gt; is a high-throughput, ultra-low latency distributed in-memory event streaming engine written in Go. Designed for large-scale telemetry ingestion, real-time message broadcasting, and event-driven microservice architectures, Ripple combines a single-threaded non-blocking I/O event loop with lock-free memory buffers to achieve high message rates while keeping CPU overhead minimal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="architecture--design"&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Design&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="architecture--design"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#architecture--design" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div role="img" aria-label="Diagram"&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid hx:mt-6"&gt;
flowchart LR
Producer[&amp;#34;Event Producers / Apps&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt;|&amp;#34;Custom TCP Protocol&amp;#34;| EventLoop[&amp;#34;Non-Blocking I/O Event Loop&amp;#34;]
subgraph RippleCore[&amp;#34;Ripple Server Engine&amp;#34;]
EventLoop --&amp;gt; Demux[&amp;#34;Message Demultiplexer&amp;#34;]
Demux --&amp;gt; TopicA[&amp;#34;Topic A Partition 0&amp;#34;]
Demux --&amp;gt; TopicB[&amp;#34;Topic A Partition 1&amp;#34;]
Demux --&amp;gt; TopicC[&amp;#34;Topic B Partition 0&amp;#34;]
TopicA --&amp;gt; MemRing[&amp;#34;In-Memory Ring Buffers&amp;#34;]
TopicB --&amp;gt; MemRing
TopicC --&amp;gt; MemRing
end
MemRing --&amp;gt; PushStream[&amp;#34;Zero-Copy Push Dispatcher&amp;#34;]
PushStream --&amp;gt; Consumer1[&amp;#34;Consumer Group Alpha&amp;#34;]
PushStream --&amp;gt; Consumer2[&amp;#34;Consumer Group Beta&amp;#34;]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="core-innovations"&gt;Core Innovations&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="core-innovations"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#core-innovations" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-Threaded Non-Blocking I/O&lt;/strong&gt;: Eliminates thread context-switching overhead and multi-threaded mutex lock contention on the hot path by processing network frames sequentially on an optimized event loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Memory Ring Buffers&lt;/strong&gt;: Employs circular memory structures with zero-copy slice slicing for message ingestion and fan-out consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Wire Protocol&lt;/strong&gt;: Lightweight binary framing over raw TCP avoids the heavy serialization overhead and HTTP/2 framing tax associated with gRPC and REST.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partitioned Topic Queues&lt;/strong&gt;: Supports horizontal stream partitioning to allow parallel consumption across independent consumer worker pools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="ecosystem-components"&gt;Ecosystem Components&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="ecosystem-components"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#ecosystem-components" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;ripple-server&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The core messaging engine handling client connections, partition management, and message dispatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;go-client&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: An ergonomic, production-grade Go SDK for producing and consuming message streams with automatic connection pooling and reconnect handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;benchmark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: A high-concurrency performance benchmarking and stress-testing tool evaluating throughput, p99 latency, and saturation points against Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
